## Continuation Update 12 (2026-04-15)
- Continued staging-flow robustness/performance work with Windows-focused primitives and copy-path optimizations:
  - Added scan backend abstraction in `src/scan.rs`:
    - `ScanBackend` enum (`StdFs`, `Win32FindFirstEx`)
    - `active_scan_backend()` platform selection
    - `scan_source_with_backend(...)` explicit backend entrypoint
  - Kept deterministic scan ordering and `.caravan` exclusion guarantees.
  - Added Windows scanner path using `FindFirstFileExW` + `FIND_FIRST_EX_LARGE_FETCH`.
  - Added scan backend tests in `tests/scan_tests.rs` for platform-aware backend selection and deterministic ordering.
- Continued copy-path performance tuning:
  - Extended `FileCopier` with `copy_file_with_size_hint(...)`.
  - Updated `copy_batch_with_components(...)` to pass planned file sizes as hints.
  - Updated `HybridFileCopier` to use the hint and avoid extra `metadata()` syscall when size is already known from planning.
  - Added regression test in `tests/transfer_tests.rs` to assert per-file planned size hints are passed to the copier.
