## Continuation Update 15 (2026-04-15)
- Continued Windows staging diagnostics hardening for capacity preflight/tracing:
  - Extended `SpaceInfo` in `src/capacity.rs` to retain both:
    - `available_bytes` (bytes available to caller)
    - `volume_free_bytes` (total free bytes on volume)
  - On Windows (`GetDiskFreeSpaceExW`), now records all three raw values into capacity reporting:
    - total bytes
    - caller-available bytes
    - volume-free bytes
  - On non-Windows (`fs2`), now records `free_space` (fallback to `available_space` on error).
  - Extended `CapacityReport` with:
    - `volume_free_bytes`
    - `probe_backend`
  - Added richer decision tracing in `format_capacity_decision_trace(...)`:
    - `destination_resolved`
    - `probe_backend`
    - `total_capacity_raw_bytes`
    - `available_raw_bytes`
    - `volume_free_raw_bytes`
    - `available_minus_reserve_raw_bytes`
    - `required_raw_bytes`
    - `planned_raw_bytes`
    - `reserve_raw_bytes`
    - `headroom_raw_bytes`
    - explicit `decision_rule` and `decision_reason`
  - Kept existing trace keys to avoid breaking downstream log parsing.
- Added/updated tests in `tests/capacity_tests.rs`:
  - New assertion coverage for probe + decision-breakdown trace fields.
  - Updated test probe fixture to provide `volume_free_bytes`.
- Validation after this phase:
  - `cargo fmt --all`: pass
  - `cargo test -q`: pass
  - `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`: pass

## Continuation Update 16 (2026-04-15)
- Continued staging preflight hardening with Windows-specific free-space divergence warnings:
  - Extended preflight destination probing in `src/preflight.rs`:
    - added `DestinationSpaceSnapshot`
    - extended `DestinationProbe` with `destination_space(...)` (default `None`)
    - implemented `SystemDestinationProbe::destination_space(...)` using capacity `SystemSpaceProbe`
  - Added warning classification:
    - `PreflightWarningCode::SpaceAccountingDivergence`
  - Added Windows-targeted divergence heuristic for warnings when:
    - `volume_free_bytes > available_bytes`
    - absolute delta is large (>= 8 GiB)
    - available-to-caller is significantly below volume-free
  - Warning message now includes raw values (`available_to_caller`, `volume_free`, `delta`) and clarifies that caravan capacity checks use caller-available bytes.
- Added integration tests in `tests/preflight_tests.rs`:
  - warns for strong Windows-style divergence (`D:\...` with large delta)
  - does not warn when values are close
- Validation after this phase:
  - `cargo fmt --all`: pass
  - `cargo test -q`: pass
  - `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`: pass

